---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Action from '../components/Action.astro';
---
<Layout title="Contribute a resource" description="Suggest a useful GitHub repository, improve selection notes, or help maintain the Awesome Repositories catalog." breadcrumbs={[{name:'Contribute',path:'/contribute/'}]}><header class="page-heading"><div class="eyebrow">GOOD FINDS ARE BETTER SHARED</div><h1>Bring your next great find.</h1><p>Help someone else find their starting point. Every contribution begins with a pull request.</p></header><article class="prose"><h2>Add a repository</h2><ol><li>Search the catalog and previous pull requests for duplicates.</li><li>Choose the most relevant existing README category.</li><li>Add one repository, alphabetically, using its original GitHub About description and correct license link.</li><li>Open a PR titled <code>Add repository-name</code> and explain why the resource is useful.</li></ol><p><Action variant="primary" href="https://github.com/pawelborkar/awesome-repos/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Read the contribution guide ↗</Action></p><h2>Share selection notes</h2><p>Tell us who a resource helps, what you can do with it, and what a newcomer should know before starting. Include source links and avoid unsupported claims about quality or experience level.</p><h2>Correct an entry</h2><p>Licenses, repository names, and documentation change. Open a correction with the source of the updated information. The README remains the catalog's source of truth.</p></article></Layout>
